          <Pad Id="KQUlMqmzKY3PoYWgV4PT5F" Bounds="-620,-60,540,1100" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="04 - The shortest line between.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Two shapes now: a seeded one that stays, and a small cloud of points that travels with&#xD;&#xA;your cursor as a polygon. The orange line always connects their two NEAREST POINTS, and&#xD;&#xA;Distance is the length of exactly that line. Distance is not just a number - it is a&#xD;&#xA;place with two ends, and neither end is a centre or a corner you chose.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;WATCH BOTH ANCHORS. Each slides along its own edge, waits at a corner while you swing&#xD;&#xA;past, then commits to the next one - on both shapes at once. Nobody programmed that;&#xD;&#xA;it falls out of what 'nearest' means.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;TOUCH. Overlap the shapes: Distance snaps to zero and the line has nowhere to go.&#xD;&#xA;Chapter 03 and this one are the same fact from two sides - Intersects true means&#xD;&#xA;Distance zero. (The cursor cloud often self-intersects, by the way. Distance does not&#xD;&#xA;care; some later operations will.)&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;THE BRIDGE OPENS BOTH WAYS. 01-03 turned Vector2 into Coordinate; here Nearest Points&#xD;&#xA;hands Coordinates back, and Split + Vector (Join) return them to Skia for drawing.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;PLAY: turn SEED - the standing shape rerolls. COUNT drives its corners and your cloud's&#xD;&#xA;points alike, one pad for both. Wire Distance somewhere - a Radius, a volume, a blur:&#xD;&#xA;proximity as a live signal is half of interactive spatial design. Units here are canvas&#xD;&#xA;units and honest, because you own this space; on lon/lat the same node returns degrees,&#xD;&#xA;not metres - Act II makes that trap visible.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;This patch uses ONE package, VL.NetTopologySuite - the geometry act's exemption: a&#xD;&#xA;course with a hole in its opening act is worse than a node appearing in two places.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;NEXT - three directions, no order:&#xD;&#xA;  Tutorial 05   grow a shape - geometry that generates geometry&#xD;&#xA;  Tutorial 03   the yes/no version of this question&#xD;&#xA;  Tutorial 06   the earth, when you are ready for it">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">11</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
